# Keep in git: instructions (CLAUDE.md, science-video-instructions.md, README.md), each video's plan.md and
# script.md, delivery notes, parts lists, captions (.srt) and all source code (html, js, py, fonts, three.js),
# so any computer can rebuild a video. Keep out: anything large or regenerated.

# Python environment: recreate it (see README)
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Rendered video and large files
*.mp4
*.mov
*.zip
*.bin

# The textbook PDF (36 MB, the NCTB book): download it again (see README)
*.pdf

# Render output that can be regenerated from the part files
**/out/send/
**/out/*.png
**/out/*.jpg
**/out/*.log
**/out/info.json
**/out/list.txt

# OS and editor files
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# check pictures made while comparing hands
/hand-*.png

*.stackdump
